{"total_count":1,"incomplete_results":false,"items":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1165","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1165/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1165/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1165/events","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1165","id":6267710117,"node_id":"I_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABdZWqpQ","number":1165,"title":"Provide explicit content-bound admission for genuinely new reviewed SSSOM owners","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-11-08T04:48:18Z","updated_at":"2026-11-08T04:48:18Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"The complete unmatched-source campaign is preparing evidence-backed proposals for genuinely new ingredient owners. At reviewed dependency #1158 head `e000d66dd26ab053e9b17ce7bf8d3c873c3dde99`, native receipts can record these new owners and canonical rows, but the release assembler intentionally has no positive admission route for several new-row shapes. They correctly default to `WITHHOLD`; this issue is a capability prerequisite, not a claim that refusal is a defect.\n\nVerified boundaries:\n\n- A new local stock identity with nonempty `other` cannot use the bare-local exception, even if every qualified token has been reviewed.\n- An entirely new CAS identity / broader ontology parent / local registry triplet cannot use `FormFollowups`: its parent and CAS claims require real predecessor positions and archived prior owner bytes. Only the added registry handle may lack a prior basis.\n- A new exact CHEBI or MICRO identity row has no positive added-row route. A general review bundle alone is not registered release authority.\n\nThe prior #1070 decision concerns retained CAS-primary forms and explicitly preserves these legacy safeguards. #850 requires approval of exact archived owner bytes. Neither authorizes new-owner support by analogy.\n\nIf positive release of these campaign rows is pursued, implement a separate, explicitly registered, closed admission document binding the native `new_record` receipt, every added row, exact integrated owner bytes, individual scientific claims, primary captures, complete token review and applicable prior negatives. Preserve distinct stock/supplied-form identities, source-qualified alias scope, CAS triplet claim independence, supported B1 siblings and withdrawal after any later owner/row change. Mapping admission must not approve roles, components or whole records.\n\nKeep all existing gates unchanged. Test actual native assembly and export with positives for each supported shape, plus missing/extra claims, fabricated history, wrong form/parent/namespace, unsafe aliases, unresolved negatives, stale or changed-and-restored inputs, missing B1 and duplicate authority. Obtain independent review before using any new path.\n\nDo not remove legitimate aliases to fit the bare-row exception, simulate retained history, change grades to evade refusal, omit required rows or hand-author a supported export ledger. Until a valid reviewed path exists, preserve these rows as withheld and report that limitation.\n\nSource-bound analysis: `.temp/all-unmatched-20261107/preflight/new-owner-admission-v1/README.md`, SHA256 `97aa629e32b05000dd5140fb02413d2d135794262651a4a5c0009b17a8036184`; manifest SHA256 `4d09ec7aae735df9bdba4243a2d98d65916d819665787b24a6cd6ab734d642af`. Seventeen source files were checked against the exact dependency commit; a separate code read agrees. This was static characterization, not a test run or scientific approval. No native code, record, mapping, workflow or gate has changed for this issue.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1165/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1165/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0}],"search_type":"lexical"}